	(text "D7 + Q2: with 5 V present VSYS comes through D7 and Q2 is off;\nwithout it Q2 turns on and the cell feeds VSYS. The charger never carries the load.\nVBAT_SENSE = VBAT / 2 (1M/1M, ~2 uA). RAIL_EN low (default, R21) = both rails off.\n+5V_SW only exists while USB or 12 V is present (no boost from the cell)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 654.05 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "021a375a-30b1-5430-b6fe-d5fd6def9546")
	)
	(text "USB-C INPUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 46.99 35.6973 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "03d2e3d5-dfa5-518e-be92-ebfb00b37124")
	)
	(text "D2 blocks reverse polarity; D3 (SMAJ15A) clamps surges. 15 V max input.\nV12_SENSE = 12 V x 100k/660k: 2.27 V at 15 V, inside the ADC range (D23).\nAP63205: fixed 5 V out. L1/C6/C7 to be checked against the datasheet (D25)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.57 97.79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1ba16c1a-07bb-547c-ad7b-542de91205fe")
	)
	(text "12 V INPUT, PROTECTION & 5 V BUCK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 36.2417 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "352a7b3b-3905-5c65-9160-30f3af15bf3d")
	)
	(text "SYSTEM POWER: LOAD SHARING, 3.3 V LDO, SWITCHED RAILS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 634.748 35.435 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "486a291a-026f-5400-901c-e82a1199db53")
	)
	(text "SENSOR PORTS: I2C, OLED, GPIO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.0853 182.755 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "50749894-c807-51a9-8e1b-6399b6f68fff")
	)
	(text "RS485 (DIRECTION FROM TX)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 384.0139 182.755 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "517fad63-5b07-59c9-bd0b-f68454b13e8e")
	)
	(text "CC1/CC2: 5.1k each to GND (USB-C sink, 5 V only).\nFit R3/R4 for an ESP32-C6 module, R5/R6 (DNP) for a C3 module:\nthe two modules have USB on different pads (DECISIONS D15/D19)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 57.15 123.19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "54505d69-57a1-5038-9f0c-a01871916cf3")
	)
	(text "Pads marked [C6]/[C3] differ between the two modules (D15, D18).\nEverything essential uses pads that work on both; BTN2 and GPIO_A/B work\nonly with a C6. SW2 is BOOT and BTN1 (IO9 strap). IO8/IO9 must be high at reset.\nC17/C18 close to module pin 3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 323.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6645d6d3-fc85-5d43-ab2a-47309ef72408")
	)
	(text "DI is tied low: the driver only ever sends 0, gated by TX through Q9.\nA 1 (and idle) is held by the 680R bias pair. Fine for Modbus at 9600 baud;\nmarginal with termination at both cable ends (D21). Bridge JP3 at a bus end.\nTransceiver, bias and pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so RS485 is off with the rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 412.75 293.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "7241dee5-b42e-57bf-9281-7e27cbaaed16")
	)
	(text "LI-ION CHARGER & CELL PROTECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 475.4831 35.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "751840f1-c586-592d-b982-40a8e0c2f803")
	)
	(text "ESP32-C6 / C3 MODULE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.0083 182.755 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "82f8ca19-daa7-5e17-81e3-107d9a772b9f")
	)
	(text "PROG: I = 1200 / R. 4.7k = 255 mA; bridge JP1 (2.35k) = 510 mA (D12).\nTEMP: JP2 bridged disables the NTC input. For a cell NTC, cut JP2 and fit\nR11 + J3 with values from the TP4056 datasheet (D27).\nJ4 (JST-PH): pin 1 = cell -, pin 2 = cell +. JST-PH polarity is not standardised:\ncheck each cell before connecting (D28).\nProtection (DW01A + FS8205A) sits in the cell's negative lead: board GND is the pack's P-."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 485.14 43.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "96755837-36ce-523c-b268-31c4c2fcc9d4")
	)
	(text "VALVE DRIVERS (LOW-SIDE MOSFET PER VALVE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 47.8871 350.395 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d3384f41-fa11-5138-941c-bb8062550f13")
	)
	(text "TCA9534 pins start as inputs; the 100k pull-downs then hold every valve off until\nfirmware drives them. Address 0x20 (A0-A2 low). P0-P7 high = valve 1-8 on.\nValves 5-8 may be left unfitted (FET, pull-down, diode, LED, resistor, terminal) (D75).\nValves: 12 V DC, low-side switched, up to ~2 A each (D73); total from 12 V IN is\nlimited by D1 (SS34, 3 A). Not for latching valves or 24 V AC valves.\nFLYBACK (D69): each diode returns to the same +12V as its valve's V+ pin, after D1.\nA valve wired to any other supply loses its clamp."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 516.89 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ec031372-9d9d-593d-b568-dc6fc3f05489")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so nothing back-powers sensors when the rail is off.\nFirmware must switch +3V3_SW on before ANY I2C traffic, including valve changes:\nthe TCA9534 (on always-on 3V3) holds its outputs meanwhile (D20). OLED shares the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 298.45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f9fc0134-d0bf-5508-a950-5c87b934d31a")
	)
